{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_binding","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_binding","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Invertible","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_weighted_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_weighted_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L93-L103","doc":"**Weighted extremal cancellation** with equal one-dimensional\nWedderburn weights `W_sym = W_alt = W`.\n\nBecause the two one-dimensional channels carry the same Plancherel\nweight, the weighted sum factors as `W · (χ_sym + χ_alt)`, which\nvanishes by `confined_knot_extremal_cancellation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_extremal_cancellation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.confined_knot_extremal_cancellation","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L76-L91","doc":"**Extremal cancellation of the symmetric crossing.**\n\nFor the symmetric mixing `(c, d) = (1, −H_A/2)`, the symmetric and\nalternating one-dimensional channels are negatives of each other, so\n`χ_sym + χ_alt = 0`.  Since the Wedderburn weights of the two\none-dimensional irreps coincide (`W_sym = W_alt`, both `= q²/(q⁴ +\n4q² + 1)`), the weighted contribution `W_sym·χ_sym + W_alt·χ_alt`\nvanishes — the binding volume is carried entirely by the standard\nrepresentation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiAlt_symmetric_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiAlt_symmetric_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L64-L74","doc":"**Alternating-channel value at the symmetric crossing.**\nAt `(c, d) = (1, −H_A/2)`, `χ_alt = −(q² + 1)/(2q)`, written division-free as\n`−((q² + 1)·⅟2·q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiSym_symmetric_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiSym_symmetric_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L52-L62","doc":"**Symmetric-channel value at the symmetric crossing.**\nAt `(c, d) = (1, −H_A/2)`, `χ_sym = (q² + 1)/(2q)`, written division-free as\n`(q² + 1)·⅟2·q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiAlt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiAlt","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L48-L50","doc":"Alternating-channel character of a crossing `(c, d)`:\n`χ_alt(c, d) = −c·q⁻¹ + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chiSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chiSym","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L44-L46","doc":"Symmetric-channel character of a crossing `(c, d)`:\n`χ_sym(c, d) = c·q + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeHA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeHA","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/confined_knot_binding.lean#L41-L42","doc":"The Hecke deformation parameter `H_A = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}